        "id": 24005
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-24T19:23:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since ldap search query has id_attr, ldap search result(res) is expected to have only one user object which is in res[0\n\nAnother reason why I have passed whole result(res) instead of res[0] \u003d\u003d\u003e result(res) is of type \u003clist\u003e containing list of user tuple objects i.e. res[0] is of type \u003ctuple\u003e. So if we pass res[0] instead of res then _filter_ldap_result_by_attr() method needs to filter user objects based on its ldap_result argument type. So I felt passing whole result(res) would be better to avoid unnecessary logic based on ldap_result argument type in _filter_ldap_result_by_attr().",
      "parentUuid": "ff346bd7_2e21a0fc",
      "revId": "b1a03e22fec0e155e87ed5bac2eff895822c10fe",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
